.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt HARNESSATOR.TOML 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm harnessator.toml
.Nd harnessator project configuration and source manifests
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
files come in two kinds, discriminated by the mandatory
.Ic kind
key.
Top-level scalars must precede table arrays
.Pq the loader rejects the TOML scoping trap explicitly .
Unknown or misplaced keys fail validation; comments are supported
(though commands that rewrite project configs re-render canonically and
drop hand-written comments).
.Sh PROJECT CONFIG (kind = "project")
Committed at the project root; its directory is the project root for all
generated artifacts.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic kind = Nq project , Ic schema = Ar int
required; schema is 1 in this release.
.It Ic targets = Ar list
harnesses to render:
.Ar opencode , claude , codex , antigravity , pi , cursor
(MVP) or planned
.Ar gemini , cline , copilot , windsurf .
Non-empty, unique.
.It Ic templates = Ar list
profile references
.Dq Ar source:profile ,
expanded in order.
Unknown profiles are validation errors.
.It Ic personal = Ar path
optional local fallback for the personal layer when no personal git
source is configured.
.It Xo Ic [[source]] No blocks:
.Ic name Ar id ,
.Ic git Ar url ,
.Ic ref Ar expr ,
.Ic layer Ar name Ic optional Xo
.Pq corporate|team|project|personal
.Xc ,
.Ic manifest Ar path Ic optional
.Xc
declared sources.
Names are unique ids; refs are tag ranges or branch names
(see Xr harnessator 1 , Sx DESCRIPTION ) .
.Ic manifest
selects a sub-directory manifest for multi-source repos
.Pq repo-relative dir or file ,
default
.Pa harnessator.toml
at the checkout root ) ;
source identity is the triple
.Pa (git , ref , manifest) .
.It Ic [select.<category>]
per-category refinement:
.Ic include Ar list ,
.Ic exclude Ar list .
Entries:
.Dq Ar cat-scope ids
bare
.Pq binds to the first declaring source, sorted by name ,
qualified
.Dq Ar source:id ,
or
.Dq *
(everything in the category).
Excludes apply last and cannot remove
.Em always
rules.
.It Ic [provider]
.Ic profile = Nq source:provider/id
- the approved model catalog to render.
.It Ic [policy]
.Ic profiles = Ar list
- policy components in override order (later wins per key).
Strict enforcement is default.
.It Ic [corporate]
.Ic allowlist Ar list No of git URL patterns Pq trailing ** wildcard ,
.Ic "lock-mode" = Nq strict | soft .
Advisory client-side; enforced by
.Nm Cm verify
in CI (policy + CI, per governance model).
.El
.Ss Example
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kind = "project"
schema = 1

targets   = ["opencode", "claude"]
templates = ["corp:default", "devops:jira-flow"]

[[source]]
name  = "corp"
git   = "https://git.example.com/ai/corp-tools.git"
ref   = "~v1.2"
layer = "corporate"

[[source]]
name  = "roland"
git   = "https://git.example.com/users/roland/tools.git"
ref   = "main"
layer = "personal"

[select.skill]
exclude = ["corp:slack-skill"]

[provider]
profile = "corp:provider/litellm-acme"

[policy]
profiles = ["corp:policy/models-approved"]

[corporate]
allowlist = ["https://git.example.com/**"]
lock-mode = "strict"
.Ed
.Sh "SOURCE MANIFEST (kind = source)"
Committed at the root of every component source repository; registers its
components, profiles and imported child sources.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic kind = Nq source , Ic schema = Ar 1
required.
.It Ic [package]
.Ic name Ar id
(required - the id refs use),
.Ic description ,
.Ic version
(informational; releases are git tags),
.Ic license ,
.Ic homepage .
.It Xo Ic [[source]] No blocks
.Xc
imported child sources, same fields as project sources - corporate roots
form source graphs.
.It Ic [profiles.<name>]
category arrays
.Pq singular names:
rule , skill , prompt , workflow , agent , hook , tool , mcp , provider ,
policy .
Values are component ids or
.Dq * .
.It Xo Ic [component.<category>."<id>"] No blocks:
.Ic path Ar rel ,
.Ic key Ar string No optional ,
.Ic description ,
.Ic tags ,
.Ic targets ,
.Ic requires ,
.Ic capabilities ,
.Ic always Ic bool No optional ,
.Ic origin Ar string No optional ,
.Ic hint.<target> tables No optional
.Xc
Component registry.
.Ic path
is repo-relative (file for prompt/workflow/rule/hook/tool-file;
directory for skill, or a convention dir for agent:
.Pa agents/<target>/<id>.md ) .
.Ic key
selects one entry inside a shared file (mcp
.Pa servers.json ) .
.Ic targets
empty = every harness;
.Ic capabilities
from
.Ar network|exec|fs ;
.Ic requires
names harness features for the capability matrix;
.Ic always
is rules-only and makes the component unexcludable.
.Ic hint.<target>
carries adapter data, e.g.
.Ic hint.cursor No globs = Pq Ar patterns ,
.Ic "hint.cursor always-apply" Ar bool .
.Ic origin
records where a component was harvested from (set by
.Cm harvest ;
not a hand-edited field).
.El
.Ss "Example"
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kind = "source"
schema = 1

[package]
name        = "corp-tools"
description = "Corporate best-practice agent configuration"
license     = "Apache-2.0"

[profiles.default]
rule  = ["security-baseline"]
skill = ["*"]

[component.rule."security-baseline"]
path        = "rules/security-baseline.md"
description = "Baseline security rules for all repos."
tags        = ["core", "security"]
always      = true

[component.rule."security-baseline".hint.cursor]
globs        = ["**/*.go"]
always-apply = true

[component.mcp."jira"]
path = "mcp/servers.json"
key  = "jira"
.Ed
.Sh "PROVIDER PROFILE (component file, providers/*.toml)"
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic name Ar id , Ic default_model Ar alias|id
catalog identity and the rendered default.
.It Ic auth_env Ar NAME
env var NAME fallback for endpoints without their own override.
.It Ic [models]
alias = concrete model id pairs - the approved catalog.
Alias and concrete spellings match each other in policies.
.It Xo Ic [styles.FAMILY] :
.Ic base_url , Ic auth_env Pq optional override
.Xc
one endpoint per API family - at least one required.
Known families:
.Ic openai-compatible ,
.Ic anthropic-compatible ,
.Ic openai-responses .
Governance dialects pick the first family their harness speaks
(opencode prefers
.Ic openai-compatible ,
claude only
.Ic anthropic-compatible ,
codex the OpenAI families),
so a gateway exposing several families at different paths renders to each
harness natively.
The old product-keyed blocks
.Pq Ic [opencode] , Ic [claude] , Ic [codex]
are rejected as unknown keys.
.El
Secret values never appear in these files - env var names only.
.Sh "POLICY (component file, policies/*.toml)"
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic strict Ar bool
default true; blocks setup on violations when true, warns otherwise.
.It Ic allowed Ar list
aliases or concrete ids admitted by the selected provider; every entry
must exist in the catalog.
.It Ic subagent_model Ar alias|id
pinned model for sub-agents (e.g. Claude Code
.Ev CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL ) .
.It Ic reason Ar text
human note shown in
.Nm Cm provider show .
.El
.Pp
Policies listed in
.Ic [policy].profiles
merge left to right, later wins per key - every relaxation stays a named
component with provenance.
.Sh "SEE ALSO"
.Xr harnessator 1 ,
.Xr harnessator.lock 5
